Tests for sial2opc.py written while fixing it (October 2026).

Each .b test prints results that are compared with the output of the same
program run natively under cintsys; the native output is in <name>.expected.

  cmptest.b     Signed comparisons, as values (LET t = a<b) and as conditional
                jumps (TEST a<b), for every pair of 11 edge values including
                32767/-32768, where a 16 bit subtraction overflows. Also constant
                shifts that the -o optimiser rewrites. Use on OPC6 and OPC7.
  optest.b      Opcodes added 23/10/2026: ikl (STATIC +:=), goto (computed
                GOTO), selld/selst/xselst (SLCT field selectors within 16 bits).
                Prints low 16 bits only, so use on OPC6 and OPC7.
  optest32.b    32 bit selector fields and large ikl constants, which need the
                large constant register r8. OPC7 only.
  writefmt.b    writef formats in the OPC bcpllib (extended 23/10/2026): widths
                before the letter (%11i), after it (%i5, %ib), %d and %n.mD
                fixed point. Use on OPC6 and OPC7.
  flt.b         Uses floating point; sial2opc.py must stop with an error
                (exit status 1) naming the unsupported opcode.
  jge0m_mlab_nop.sial
                Hand-written SIAL for jge0m, mlab and nop, which the current
                compiler no longer generates. Check the translation by eye:
                  python3 ../../bcpl/sial2opc.py --opc7 -n -f jge0m_mlab_nop.sial -g ../../bcpl/ext_sial.h

Running the tests, with the BCPL environment variables set:

  make                 all tests on OPC7, printing PASS/FAIL for each
  make ARCH=opc6       the tests that fit in 16 bits, on OPC6
  make check-all       clean, OPC6, clean, OPC7 (outputs share file names,
                       so run 'make clean' when switching ARCH by hand)
  make clean

make exits non-zero if any test fails.

The steps make runs for one test (here optest on OPC7; use 6 for OPC6):

  cintsys -c bcpl2sial optest.b to optest.sial
  python3 ../../bcpl/sial2opc.py --opc7 -f optest.sial -f ../bcpltests/bcpllib.sial \
      -s ../../bcpl/opc7_syslib.s -g ../../bcpl/ext_sial.h -o > optest.tmp.s
  cat ../../include/opc7/macros.s optest.tmp.s ../../bcpl/opc7_rom.s > optest.s
  python3 ../opc7asm.py optest.s optest.hex > optest.lst
  python3 ../opc7emu.py optest.hex optest.dump | grep OUT | ../../utils/show_stdout.py --opc7 > optest.out
  diff optest.expected optest.out

For OPC6 use ../../opc6/opc6asm.py and ../../opc6/opc6emu.py, the opc6 syslib,
rom and macros, and --opc6 for show_stdout.py.

Note: write a comparison as a separate LET (LET t = a<b) to get the value
opcodes; the multiple form LET t1, t2 = a<b, a>b compiles to jumps.
